---
import FeaturesLayout from '../../layouts/FeaturesLayout.astro';
const codeBlock =
  'bg-cdx-bg-alt/60 text-cdx-text overflow-x-auto rounded-lg p-3 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed';
const inlineCode = 'text-cdx-text bg-cdx-bg-alt rounded px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.85em]';
---

<FeaturesLayout
  currentSlug="coverage"
  title="Documentation Coverage — compodocx"
  description="Per-symbol coverage report with CI gating and a JSON output dashboards can consume."
>
  <p class="text-cdx-text-secondary text-lg">
    Every run produces a coverage report — the percentage of public symbols carrying at least a
    one-line description. Below the threshold, the CLI exits non-zero so CI can gate.
  </p>

  {/* prettier-ignore */}
  <pre class:list={codeBlock}><code>npx compodocx --coverageMinimum 80</code></pre>

  <p class="text-cdx-text-secondary">
    A <code class={inlineCode}>coverage.json</code> file is also written so dashboards can ingest the
    numbers without scraping HTML. Schema:
  </p>

  {/* prettier-ignore */}
  <pre
    class:list={codeBlock}><code>{`{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "totals": { "documented": 348, "total": 412, "percentage": 84.5 },
  "byKind": {
    "components": { "documented": 42, "total": 48 },
    "directives": { "documented": 18, "total": 18 },
    "classes":    { "documented": 91, "total": 110 },
    "interfaces": { "documented": 197, "total": 236 }
  },
  "undocumented": [
    "src/cards/card-grid.component.ts:CngxCardGrid",
    "src/utils/intersection.directive.ts:CngxIntersection"
  ]
}`}</code></pre>

  <p class="text-cdx-text-secondary">
    The HTML page renders a Documentation Coverage tab on the project root — sortable, filterable by
    kind, with deep links to every undocumented symbol.
  </p>
</FeaturesLayout>
